  "id": "Compound::DB01023 - Gene::775",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between Felodipine and Cacna1c, mediated through the class of Dihydropyridines. Felodipine, as a member of this class, is included in Dihydropyridines, which in turn includes Clevidipine. Both Clevidipine and Nisoldipine, which are also part of the Dihydropyridine class, bind to Cacna1c. This indicates that Felodipine, through its inclusion in the Dihydropyridine family, exerts a functional interaction with Cacna1c. The shared lowest common ancestors—Dihydropyridine—suggest a common mechanism of action, likely involving calcium channel modulation. The evidence supports a pathway where Felodipine, as a Dihydropyridine, interacts with Cacna1c via a shared biological mechanism, reinforcing the role of calcium channel blockers in modulating neuronal activity.",
